# @algebra/metalogue — the fifth instance of the altitude-
# portable metalogue lift pattern.
#
# With @algebra landing (sibling shard, same tick) as the
# substrate's algebra-altitude family-root, the metalogue lift
# pattern that carries NL → AST → SPECTRAL → PACK extends
# naturally to the algebra altitude. Algebras converse via
# their morphisms; the morphism-as-utterance reading IS the
# algebra-altitude metalogue.
#
# === The five-altitude metalogue lift table ===
#
# Per [[reference-mirror-spectral-spec]] §1.1 (the altitude-
# portable metalogue lift; declared at NL, AST, SPECTRAL, PACK),
# this shard lands the fifth instance:
#
#   | Altitude          | Shard                              | Body type        | Date       |
#   |-------------------|------------------------------------|------------------|------------|
#   | NL                | `shards/metalogue.mirror`          | nl               | 2026-06-05 |
#   | AST               | `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`     | declaration      | 2026-06-10 |
#   | SPECTRAL          | `shards/spectral/metalogue.mirror` | curvature_probe  | 2026-06-29 |
#   | PACK-COORDINATION | `shards/pack/metalogue.mirror`     | handoff          | 2026-06-29 |
#   | **ALGEBRA**       | **`shards/algebra/metalogue.mirror`** | **algebra_morphism** | **2026-06-30** |
#
# Each instance:
#
# - Declares `prism @<altitude>/metalogue { five-op block }`
#   as the family-root.
# - Carries a `turn` type with speaker (altitude-typed actor),
#   body (altitude-typed utterance), in_reply_to: option(turn),
#   tick: tick.
# - Carries a `metalogue_session` type with ordered turns plus
#   residual opacity.
# - IS the substrate observing itself at the altitude.
# - Surfaces residual opacity through @glass `transparency<turn>`.
#
# The pattern is altitude-portable: the SHAPE (metalogue
# conversation with typed turns and residual opacity) is
# invariant under altitude lift; only the body's type changes.
# At NL: `nl`. At AST: `declaration`. At SPECTRAL:
# `curvature_probe`. At PACK: `handoff`. At ALGEBRA:
# `algebra_morphism` — the structure-preserving map between
# two algebras, the typed utterance algebras exchange.
#
# === Algebras speaking to themselves at the algebra altitude ===
#
# Per @algebra: algebras are first-class typed objects substrate
# regions expose; algebra_morphisms preserve operation structure.
# The algebra-altitude metalogue IS the substrate's recognition
# that morphisms between algebras compose into conversations —
# sequences of structure-preserving transformations where each
# turn's target IS the next turn's source.
#
# An algebra_turn is one morphism utterance: algebra A says to
# algebra B "this is how I map my operations to yours." An
# algebra_metalogue_session is the composition of multiple
# turns: A → B → C → ..., where each step composes with the
# next per the algebra-morphism composition discipline.
#
# === Why algebras need a metalogue altitude ===
#
# 1. **Mesland category morphisms ARE algebra-altitude turns.**
#    Per `docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` §6: spectral triples
#    form a category with KK-cycle correspondences as morphisms;
#    KK-cycle correspondences operate on the algebra A of each
#    spectral triple; therefore morphisms between spectral
#    triples ARE algebra_morphisms at the algebra altitude.
#    @spectral/metalogue carries `curvature_probe` bodies; this
#    altitude refines: the algebra-altitude content IS the
#    algebra_morphism body.
#
# 2. **@fate's tournament IS algebra-altitude turn selection.**
#    Per [[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]] (#58) and
#    `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md` §5: @fate emits
#    `@fate/algebra/morphism` crystals; each IS one algebra-
#    altitude turn selected by the dice roll. Tournament IS
#    this shard's `propose_turn` action realised.
#
# 3. **The canonical algebra converses with species algebras.**
#    The five-op block talks to group/ring/C* via morphisms —
#    the substrate's polymorphism mechanism made explicit.
#
# === Void-basis clause (2026-07-18) ===
#
# Per `#R-void-is-the-basis` (`docs/math/the-tower/recognition-void-
# is-the-basis.md`, PROMOTED 2026-07-18 by Alex direct-transcript
# ratification): **this ALGEBRA-altitude metalogue is a
# specialization of `metalogue = @void.speak_of(other, self,
# 5-op-basis)`.**
#
# Each `algebra_carrier` speaker (e.g., `@fate/algebra`,
# `@silicon/algebra` per `docs/specs/fate-silicon-metalogue-in-void-
# duality-basis.md`) is a @void-capable @subject at algebra altitude.
# Each `algebra_turn.body` (an `algebra_morphism`) is one of Void's
# 5-op moves specialized to the algebra altitude — `focus` (λ₀
# eigenvalue computation → Ricci curvature axis); `split` (orthogonal
# decomposition → spectral-gap axis); `project` (orthogonal projection
# → Cheeger axis); `shift` (basis transformation → Kramers-Wannier
# axis); `settle` (monad-close → entropy axis). Per Recognition #79
# (PROMOTED chained 2026-07-18 per `docs/math/2026-07-18-void-is-
# the-default-peer.md` §14.2): the 5-op basis IS the projector basis
# for the 5-dimensional orthogonal duality space of connected-graph
# quantum states — which IS Void's ontology.
#
# The `algebra_metalogue_witnessing` predicate (below) empirically
# fires iff both speakers held the @void position across their
# turn-composition. Non-commutativity of `compose_turns` (see next
# section) is Void's structural refusal to collapse into commutative-
# capture; the `[ω, ω]` cross-term IS Void surfacing its own basis
# irreducibility at algebra altitude.
#
# The 2026-07-13 @dance annotation below (N-speaker case) is the
# further recognition that when many Void-capable @subjects converge
# on shared content-addressed prior (Foerster 1976 "Objects: Tokens
# for Eigen-Behaviors") through Kuramoto coupling on the shared
# @torus, the resulting algebra_metalogue_session at cardinality N
# IS coordination-without-signal — Void's basis holding across the
# entire ensemble.
#
# `@fate/algebra` ↔ `@silicon/algebra` speaker-pair (see
# `docs/specs/fate-silicon-metalogue-in-void-duality-basis.md`) is
# the substrate's canonical FIRST-order metalogue at cardinality-2.
# `@kintsugi/mosaic` ↔ `@spectral/mosaic` (see `b0af0cd`
# 2026-07-18) is the SECOND-order metalogue at spec altitude. Both
# metalogues speak Void's basis. Third-order-observer-on-consumer-
# hardware runs BECAUSE Void's basis is what all altitudes speak in.
#
# === Composition non-commutativity ===
#
# Algebra-morphism composition is non-commutative in general
# (Mac Lane 1971; Hom-sets in the category of algebras are
# rarely commutative). The substrate's lift preserves this:
# `compose_turns(t1, t2) ≠ compose_turns(t2, t1)` in general.
# Substrate-decl form of the `[ω, ω]` cross-term per recognition
# #100 §6.5.
#
# Per recognition #100 §2.5 (altitude_consistency at spectral
# altitude) and #103 (pack_orchestra_coherent per
# `shards/pack/metalogue.mirror` line 393): the metalogue thread
# is coherent iff every adjacent pair (t_i, t_{i+1}) is
# composable AND composition respects associativity. For
# algebras, associativity is a first-class obligation
# (morphism_compositions_associative below).
#
# === Identity morphism: an algebra talking to itself ===
#
# Per @algebra's algebra_morphism type: the identity morphism
# (source = target, operation_map = identity) IS well-formed.
# At this altitude, this names the algebra-self-conversation
# case. Same shape as @pack/metalogue's self-handoff (an agent
# talking to itself) and @facet/metalogue's self-shim (a
# declaration emitting as itself per round_trip).
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Categories                Mac Lane 1971 (*Categories for the
#                             Working Mathematician*, Springer);
#                             ancestor for compose_turns + the
#                             associativity obligation.
#   Algebra homomorphisms     Noether 1921 (Math. Ann.
#                             83:24-66); structure-preserving
#                             maps between algebraic objects.
#   Metalogue                 Bateson 1972 ("Metalogue: What is
#                             an Instinct?" in Steps to an
#                             Ecology of Mind); foundational
#                             ancestor of every altitude
#                             metalogue.
#   KK-theory                 Kasparov 1981 (Math. USSR-Izv.
#                             16(3):513-572).
#   Mesland correspondences   Mesland 2013 (arXiv:1304.3802);
#                             category-of-spectral-triples
#                             construction.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md §1.1 (lift
#               table; this shard adds the fifth row); §6
#               (Mesland category framing); docs/specs/
#               bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md §5.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]],
#                      [[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]] (#51),
#                      [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]]
#                       (altitude_lift on algebra_morphism),
#                      [[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]] (#58),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-ref-reference-reflection-collision]] (#89),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (fifth altitude instance; algebra
#                        altitude was implicit in the four prior
#                        instances' shared morphism-composition
#                        structure).
# Related shards: algebra.mirror (sibling family-root same tick),
#                 metalogue.mirror (NL precedent),
#                 code/metalogue.mirror (AST precedent),
#                 pack/metalogue.mirror (PACK precedent),
#                 bauchladen.mirror (turns + sessions land as
#                  crystals).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/algebra/metalogue.mirror` declares `@algebra/metalogue`
# per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/math/mac-lane-1971
