# === The algebra_turn carrier ===
#
# Typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming one move
# in an algebra-altitude metalogue. Parallel to the four prior
# instances' turn types (nl/declaration/curvature_probe/handoff),
# refined to the algebra altitude.
#
# - `speaker`     the algebra_carrier issuing the turn; the
#                 algebra "speaking" in this round. Speaker IS
#                 the algebra whose operations the body
#                 originates from.
# - `body`        the algebra_morphism the speaker utters;
#                 structure-preserving map from speaker to the
#                 algebra the turn addresses.
# - `in_reply_to` optional prior turn this one composes onto;
#                 None for opening turn, Some(t_prev) for
#                 continuation.
# - `tick`        canonical substrate monotonic clock per
#                 @epistemologic/reality/time; turns compose
#                 only with turns at strictly-greater tick.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type algebra_turn = {
  speaker:     algebra_carrier,
  body:        algebra_morphism,
  in_reply_to: option(algebra_turn),
  tick:        tick,
}

# === The algebra_metalogue_session carrier ===
#
# Per recognition #100 §2.4 (metalogue_session shape lifted to
# the algebra altitude): ordered turn sequence plus residual
# opacity. Same shape as @metalogue.metalogue_session,
# @facet/metalogue.metalogue_session, @pack/metalogue
# .metalogue_thread; lifted to the algebra altitude.
#
# - `turns`    ordered sequence of algebra-to-algebra turns.
#              Turn-order matters per non-commutative
#              composition; reordering produces a structurally
#              different session.
# - `opacity`  @glass transparency parameterized on algebra_turn;
#              every unresolved gap (a morphism that couldn't
#              fully preserve operation structure under
#              composition) is sited on a specific turn.
# - `origin`   ref to the algebra_carrier the session is centered
#              on; typically the algebra that opened the session.
#              `algebra_witnessing(origin)` MUST hold at the
#              session's species boundary.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type algebra_metalogue_session = {
  turns:   [algebra_turn],
  opacity: transparency(algebra_turn),
  origin:  ref,
}

# === propose_turn action ===
#
# Per-algebra turn realization: takes a speaker algebra_carrier
# and a body algebra_morphism (body.source MUST equal speaker —
# an algebra speaks only its own outgoing morphisms) and returns
# the algebra_turn at the current tick. Substrate-vocabulary
# primitive for naming turns at the algebra altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary. @fate's
# tournament selector IS one operational realization (per
# "Why algebras need a metalogue altitude" reason 2); future
# per-species shards (e.g., @algebra/c_star/metalogue) may
# realize with species-specific morphism-proposal discipline.
propose_turn(speaker: algebra_carrier, body: algebra_morphism) -> algebra_turn { \ }

# === compose_turns action ===
#
# Algebra-morphism composition at the metalogue altitude.
# Takes two turns t1, t2 such that t1.body.target =
# t2.body.source (composability: second turn's morphism must
# originate from the algebra the first delivered to) and
# returns Some(composite_turn) for the two-step composition,
# or None when composability fails.
#
# Non-commutative per "Composition non-commutativity" above:
# compose_turns(t1, t2) ≠ compose_turns(t2, t1) in general,
# because algebra-morphism composition (the [ω, ω] cross-term
# lifted to algebra altitude per recognition #100 §6.5) is
# non-commutative under most algebras' composition discipline.
# Returning option(algebra_turn) surfaces the composability
# check at the type level per [[feedback-no-bare-types]];
# consumers MUST match on Some/None.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; composite
# morphism is computed via @algebra.compose on the source
# algebra's operations.
compose_turns(t1: algebra_turn, t2: algebra_turn) -> option(algebra_turn) { \ }

# === session_well_formed predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict (per recognition #37, Pask-agreement) that
# an algebra_metalogue_session is structurally well-formed:
# every adjacent pair (t_i, t_{i+1}) is composable
# (t_i.body.target = t_{i+1}.body.source); every turn's
# speaker matches its body's source; every turn's tick is
# strictly greater than the prior; the origin algebra satisfies
# `algebra_witnessing(s.origin)` at the species boundary.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary.
session_well_formed(s: algebra_metalogue_session) -> verdict { \ }

# === The bilateral requires obligations ===
#
# Per the canonical metalogue-altitude discipline (precedent at
# @facet/metalogue + @pack/metalogue + the canonical spec at
# `docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md` §2.5): consumer shards
# declare bilateral agreement by writing the obligations below.

# The session follows the altitude-portable lift pattern.
# Inheritor shards discharge by ensuring their algebra-altitude
# metalogue session honors the five-altitude lift signature
# (parallel turn/session structure to the four prior instances):
# turns are typed records; session carries residual opacity
# through @glass transparency; origin is content-addressed;
# body type is algebra_morphism (not arbitrary substrate refs).
# Discipline obligation that keeps the fifth altitude
# instance structurally consistent with the prior four.
algebra_inherits_metalogue_lift(s: algebra_metalogue_session) -> verdict { \ }

# Algebra-morphism composition IS associative under the
# substrate's composition rule. For any three composable turns
# t1, t2, t3:
#
#   compose_turns(compose_turns(t1, t2), t3)
#   = compose_turns(t1, compose_turns(t2, t3))
#
# (modulo option(.) wrapping). Associativity per Mac Lane 1971
# §I.1; algebra-altitude form of the substrate's morphism-
# composition associativity discipline.
morphism_compositions_associative(turns: [algebra_turn]) -> verdict { \ }

# === The algebra_metalogue_witnessing inheritance predicate ===
#
# `algebra_metalogue_witnessing(s)` is the predicate consumer
# shards name in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral
# agreement that session `s` satisfies all three obligations
# above conjointly: session_well_formed +
# algebra_inherits_metalogue_lift +
# morphism_compositions_associative.
#
# Same shape as @pack/metalogue.pack_metalogue_witnessing(t)
# and the metalogue family's `requires substrate_pull_preserving
# (shim_X)` pattern at `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`. Composes
# per-turn well-formedness with thread-level lift-pattern with
# associativity into one inheritance contract.
#
# Forward-promised inheritors:
#
# - `@fate/algebra/morphism` (forward-promised per
#   `docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md` §5): each
#   @fate-emitted algebra_morphism crystal IS one turn in the
#   algebra metalogue; the sub-shard declares `requires
#   algebra_metalogue_witnessing(emitted_session)` when its
#   tournament composes multiple selections.
# - `@spectral/metalogue` species refinements: when the
#   spectral-altitude curvature_probe body is refined to expose
#   its algebra-altitude content explicitly, the refinement
#   consumes algebra_metalogue_witnessing on the underlying
#   algebra session.
# - `@algebra/<species>/metalogue` (forward-promised): species-
#   specific metalogues (group, ring, C*-algebra metalogues)
#   inherit and refine the predicate for their species'
#   morphism-composition discipline.
algebra_metalogue_witnessing(s: algebra_metalogue_session) -> verdict { \ }

